  "rationale": "The plant separates sensing and motion: G1 models the robot's perception (uncontrollable events), G2 models the robot's motion capabilities (controllable events). The main specification E1 binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and ensuring steady exploration. E2 prevents repeated recovery actions (e.g., no repeated move_backward or full_rotate).",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect open-loop actuation and sensor-driven transitions.",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent oscillatory or repeated recovery behaviors."
